From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:23:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] soc: mediatek: Add the MT6878 GNSS data link driver

The AP side of the GNSS DSPs of the MT6878 CONNSYS (CONFIG_MTK_GPS_DL):
/dev/gpsdl0 and /dev/gpsdl1 for the GNSS navigation daemon, each a byte
stream over DMA rings in the CONNSYS EMI, with the power and data-link
sequences done through the BL31 SiP service as the downstream gps_drv_dl
driver does in its TF-A build, plus the gps_emi, gps_pwr and gps2scp
devices the daemon opens. When the boot loader does not write "emi-addr"
into the node, the GNSS EMI is taken right after the CONNSYS EMI, as in
the factory layout. Ported from MediaTek's GPL connectivity/gps/data_link
driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
